{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion commands and perception outcomes. The specification automata encode the safe, conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are triggered by obstacle events. Recovery states deterministically select a single turn direction based on which side is blocked, and full_rotate is reserved for deadlock cases. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and controllable actions are one-shot per commit state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect the robot's architecture.",
    "Specification automata encode the safe exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward for progress, deterministic turn recovery on obstacle, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
